	quests: [
		{
			title: "Almost All Things Storage"
			x: -0.75d
			y: 0.5d
			shape: "octagon"
			description: [
				"&eAh, Explorer Eric, good to be working with you again."
				""
				"&bOh, Designer Daisy! I take it we'll be working together here to help Bandit?"
				""
				"&eSure enough. Bandit, this section is gonna cover Storage options for ya. Welllll, most of them."
				""
				"&bWhat? Why aren't we covering all the bases for them?"
				""
				"&eAh, as one of the storage mediums is headed by Dataologist..."
				""
				"&b...Dante, ah right right then. Bandit, we'll cover the 'smaller' storage options."
				""
				"&eThe stuff that doesn't involve 1s and 0s and data preservation concerns. That's Dataologist Dante's Domain."
			]
			dependencies: [
				"1D0853ADC7295AEB"
				"45A4E38A1E2BA965"
				"06FED1C3C1EA8361"
			]
			id: "4D0A9C13F67B5F1A"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2A996A56B647FF3A"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
		}
		{
			x: -2.5d
			y: 0.5d
			shape: "diamond"
			subtitle: "MOD : Pocket Storage (@pocketstorage)"
			description: [
				"&eWell, it looks like the FOP left some of their earlier work in the game... "
				""
				"&bAh, the bosses mentioned something about that."
				""
				"&eIt looks like they left an alternate inventory system?"
				""
				"&bWait... oh, I recognize that! What was it called.. Subpocket? Yeah, a near infinite capacity pocket without a grid system..."
				""
				"&e...Okay, what's the catch, Explorer Eric?"
				""
				"&bWell, you can stack item sprites atop each other very easily. And you only have so much visual space. "
				""
				"&eOh. That's an interesting tradeoff..."
				""
				"&bSeems you can use an exploit to reactivate the Subpocket. Find a Subspatial Key in a dungeon chest, then use it to break a normal Ender Chest in the End. It's very slow, and will constantly damage you until you finish, though!"
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			dependencies: ["4D0A9C13F67B5F1A"]
			id: "7B5478A65FA699B9"
			tasks: [{
				id: "193F70D76CFCD704"
				type: "item"
				item: "pocketstorage:psu_1"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "2E21EAF0EE3C01EC"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2245246540467579945L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Classic Storage"
			x: -2.5d
			y: -1.25d
			shape: "square"
			subtitle: "MOD : Iron Chests (@ironchests)"
			description: [
				"&bAh, good old Iron Chests."
				""
				"&ePretty simple, but effective. I'm surprised that the FOP didn't try to improve on it."
				""
				"&bEven bird brains got enough sense not to mess with a good thing."
				""
				"&eWell, don't underestimate them, Explorer Eric. Anyways, Bandit, Iron Chests has been a long running staple of both inside the Ferret Business and outside as well."
				""
				"&bIt's a simple tiered chest system. Wood to Copper, Copper to Iron, etc. "
				""
				"&eThey look pretty good too. And as a bonus, you can craft these Upgrades. They let you upgrade an already placed Chest, so you don't have to reorganize anything to break and replace the chest."
				""
				"&bJust Right Click the Upgrade on the appropriate Chest."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			dependencies: ["4D0A9C13F67B5F1A"]
			id: "7C2360C681B09334"
			tasks: [{
				id: "55BA7D8126898B72"
				type: "item"
				item: "ironchests:copper_chest"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "3DA86EA626D94AD5"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			x: -2.5d
			y: 2.75d
			shape: "diamond"
			subtitle: "MOD : Compressium (@compressium)"
			description: [
				"&eBandit, if you've started poking into making your own branch of The Ferret Business with Minecolonies, you have probably encountered these already. "
				""
				"&bAh, Storage Racks. Quite familiar if you go urban adventuring in old factories and warehouses."
				""
				"&eOnly visually, how they function in Minecolonies and how they function elsewhere are slightly different."
				""
				"&bHow so?"
				""
				"&eOutside of Minecolonies, you need to start with a Controller. Then you place Storage Racks so that they are touching the Controller, or can chain a connection back to the Controller."
				""
				"&bOh I see. You can then put stuff on the shelves, and use the Controller to track all the items. Neat!"
				""
				"&eYou can upgrade a placed Rack by Left Clicking it with the next material."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			dependencies: ["4D0A9C13F67B5F1A"]
			id: "5A2BE4E6B0616FB4"
			tasks: [{
				id: "74B1EC0605CEDF1C"
				type: "item"
				item: "compressium:cobblestone_1"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "1E0CEADBA4222D6F"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			x: 1.0d
			y: -1.25d
			shape: "diamond"
			subtitle: "MOD : Cloud Storage (@cloudstorage)"
			description: [
				"&bVery interesting... it looks like the FOP took some of your discoveries in your previous adventure and created an exact copycat of it. I'm talking about the Ender Storage creations we made."
				""
				"&eWait, how did they get the designs? They beat us to market it seems."
				""
				"&bOh the usual, spies and espionage. Or Bandit may have had one on them, or jotted down in notes. They 'were' lost in transit for a while."
				""
				"&eTrue...well, Bandit, if you don't remember, these Ender Chests are a bit more advanced than the normal vanilla game 'Ender Chest'. Each one has 3 dyeable spots on top. Each 3 color combination connects to a different Ender Chest."
				""
				"&bThat goes for all other assistants as well. If you want to lock an Ender Chest to a private 'chest network' only you can access, Right Click a Diamond on the lock."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			dependencies: ["4D0A9C13F67B5F1A"]
